            "review_title": "Review at Tea Avenue",
            "review_text": "Luna C\n4 contributions\n0\nTea time for two\nMay 2019 • Friends\nWhile other tea houses in Ho Chi Minh city uses supermarket product like Lipton or Twinning, Tea Avenue has its own franchise from Sri Lanka which piques our interests. So, we went there for some snacks and at the same time ordered a tea set.\n\nThe snacks we ordered, calamari rings and some chip, was crispy and delicious with the sauce provided. Unfortunately, the portion was a bit small, but that wasn't a concern since we just want to have a bit of snack before tea.\n\nThe tea set was impressive. This is the 4th tea house we visited in Ho Chi Minh city, but none could compare to this particular taste. The tea we ordered was light on taste with a hint of citrus, but somehow still retain its effectiveness on cleaning out palette after eating cake.\n\nCuriously, there was some non-sweet food on the bottom level of the tea set, which comes to us as a surprise since we mostly saw cookies, macarons and cheesecakes served in other tea houses. We were not sure if this was a service by the tea house since we ordered some salty snacks earlier, but it was a welcomed surprise.\n\nWe also bought a tin of tea which they sell similar to that of coffee from Starbucks. We didn't really need this since we are in Vietnam and should have bought locally produced tea as it would have more value as souvenirs or gifts, but I like the taste so much I couldn't help but buying it for drinking later as this isn't sold elsewhere.\n\nWe highly recommend this tea house for anyone who likes a different taste to the tea commonly served at other places in Ho Chi Minh. There is a no smoking policy indoor so keep that in mind when visiting this restaurant.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten June 5, 2019",
